+  winners and the timer are settings, imported quizzes get the defaults.
+
+### Question timer (release 4)
+
+- Settings: "Timer minutes" (0..99) and "Timer seconds" (0..59), whole numbers,
+  0 and 0 by default = no timer (`Quiz#timer_duration`, `#timer?`). An emptied
+  field counts as 0; out-of-range values show "Timer seconds must be at most 59"
+  etc. in the errors box (form is `novalidate`). Like the number of winners, the
+  timer is a setting of this Quizzy: not exported, imported quizzes get 0 / 0.
+- Deadline: when Start/Next opens a question, `Game#show!` reads the quiz's timer
+  *fresh from the database* and stores `games.question_ends_at` (opened_at +
+  duration, nil without timer). Stored, so a reload of the big screen never
+  restarts the countdown; changing the setting mid-question only affects the
+  next questions. Kept after the question closes (`question_ends_at?` = "this
+  question was timed"; `Game#timed?` = open *and* timed).
+- At the deadline the question finishes exactly like "Finish"
+  (`Game#finish_if_time_is_up!` → `finish_question!`: same state, broadcast,
+  results on screens and phones). Three ways it gets there, all idempotent:
+  1. `QuestionTimer`: a `Concurrent::ScheduledTask` in the Puma process, scheduled
+     after commit when a timed question opens. Phones get the result at 0:00 even
+     with no big screen open (measured in production: 6.0–6.2 s for a 6 s timer).
+     Scheduling is once per (game, deadline) (`QuestionTimer::PENDING`).
+  2. `Game#check_timer!` runs before every big-screen and phone request
+     (`Moderate::GamesController`, `Play::BaseController#set_game`): finishes an
+     overdue question, else makes sure its timer is scheduled in this process.
+     Timers live in memory, so after a restart the first phone/screen that
+     reconnects re-arms it (measured: server restarted 4 s into a 20 s question,
+     phone got its result at 20.4 s).
+  3. The big screen's countdown fetches its live fragment at 0:00
+     (`countdown:expired->live#refresh`, retried with backoff until the open
+     question is gone).
+- Races: the timer and a "Finish" click are ordinary optimistic-locking writers;
+  the loser gets `StaleObjectError` (ignored / reloaded), nothing is skipped. A
+  "Finish" posted with the pre-timeout version after 0:00 just redirects.
+- Late answers: `Game#answer!` refuses (409) a pick that *arrived* at or after the
+  deadline (`at >= question_ends_at`), even if the question isn't marked closed
+  yet. A pick that arrived in time but waited for the write lock past an
+  already-committed finish is refused like after "Finish".
+- Countdown (`countdown_controller.js`, big screen only): the server renders
+  `data-countdown-remaining-value` (ms left at render, from the stored deadline);
+  the browser counts down on `performance.now()` (the projector's clock may be
+  wrong), resyncing only when a fresh render changes the value (morphs, polls).
+  Whole seconds round *up*: a 5 s timer shows "0:05" at once, "0:01" in its last
+  second, and finishes at 0:00 (so "0:00" itself only flashes: the closed
+  question shows results, no timer, exactly as after "Finish"). The time left is
+  not part of `ScreenView#version` (the deadline changes with `lock_version`).
+- Tests: `QuestionTimer.enabled = false` in `test_helper.rb` (no background
+  thread touching transactional data; tests use `travel` + the request path),
+  `true` in system tests (as in production) and in `question_timer_test.rb`.
+  `travel`/`travel_to` drop sub-second precision unless `with_usec: true`.
+- Migrations: `AddQuestionTimer` only adds columns (an existing production DB
+  keeps its quizzes, games and players; checked with `bin/serve`'s `db:prepare`).
+  Careful with *rollbacks* on SQLite: `remove_column` rebuilds the table, and
+  dropping the old `quizzes` runs the `ON DELETE CASCADE` foreign keys, so
+  rolling back this (or `AddPrizes`) deletes every game.
 
